>> title: Mexican Red Rice
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: rice, tomato, mexican, side, stovetop
>> counters: Taquería, Diner
>> aka: arroz rojo, spanish rice
>> servings: 6
>> time: 45 min
>> step.1: blend smooth
>> step.2: fry 6 min
>> step.3: pour over
>> step.4: simmer covered 20 min, rest
>> step.5: fluff, fold in

Blend @plum tomatoes{2%medium}(cored), @white onion{1/4%medium}, @garlic{2%cloves}, and @chicken stock{1 3/4%cups}(415 mL) smooth in a #blender{}.

Fry @long-grain white rice{1 1/2%cups}(300 g; rinsed and drained) in @vegetable oil{3%Tbs} in a #saucepan{} until golden and nutty, ~{6%min}.

Pour @&(~2)tomato purée{} over @&(~1)toasted rice{} with @serrano chile{1}(left whole) and @kosher salt{1 1/2%tsp}.

Simmer @&(~1)pot{} covered over low heat for ~{20%min}, then rest off the heat ~{10%min}.

Fluff @&(~1)rice{} with a #fork{} and fold in @frozen peas{1/2%cup}(70 g; thawed) and @cilantro{2%Tbs}.
